{
  "$comment": "Peer dependencies per slice of @marinoscar/memoriahub-* (RETRO-J1 #593). Append-only: J2-J11 add slices, never rename or remove one. memoriahub-compute declares its libraries (sharp, onnxruntime-node, exifr, zod; optional tesseract.js) as exact-pinned dependencies, not peers, so that a server and a worker node run byte-identical native builds; every slice therefore lists no peer. Enforced by scripts/memoriahub-packages/check-slice-peers.mjs; the rules are in docs/PACKAGES.md#peer-dependencies-per-slice.",
  "$universal": {
    "memoriahub-compute": "*",
    "memoriahub-contract": "*",
    "memoriahub-db": [
      "bin"
    ],
    "memoriahub-api": [
      "ports"
    ],
    "memoriahub-web": [
      "core"
    ]
  },
